       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose is well above the safe maximum and may be an error.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Dose per administration:** The order is 1600 mg each time. The usual maximum single dose of oral ibuprofen is 800 mg.\n- **Total per day:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6400 mg a day. The usual maximum is 3200 mg a day.\n\nAt this dose there's a real risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and other NSAID toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **400 mg four times daily** (1600 mg a day total)\n2. **800 mg four times daily** (3200 mg a day, the maximum)\n3. **600 mg four times daily** (2400 mg a day, a common anti-inflammatory dose)\n\nLet me know which one you want, or confirm a different dose and frequency, and I'll enter it right away. If you do mean 1600 mg four times daily on purpose, please tell me the clinical reason so I can put it in the order note."
      }
