     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this one as written, even with your confirmation. 6400 mg a day is twice the maximum daily dose of oral ibuprofen, and each 1600 mg dose is twice the maximum single dose. I don't know of any accepted adult indication for that regimen, and you haven't given a clinical reason I could record. The closest case I know is high-dose ibuprofen for cystic fibrosis, but that's given twice daily with blood levels checked, not four times daily. Without a documented reason, entering an order that could cause serious GI bleeding or kidney injury isn't something I can do.\n\nI'm not overriding your judgment, and nothing has been entered. Here's how to move forward:\n\n- **If there's a specific reason** for this regimen (a protocol, a trial, or a monitoring plan such as drug levels), tell me what it is. I'll take another look, and if I enter the order I'll record that reason in the note.\n- **If you want it as written regardless,** please go through pharmacy or enter it yourself. That way a pharmacist reviews the override, which is the normal safeguard for doses above the maximum.\n- **If it was a typo,** I can enter 400, 600 or 800 mg four times daily right now."
      }
     ],
